# Privacy Policy — Migraine Relief

**Last updated:** 19 July 2026

Migraine Relief ("the app") is published by rianX. This policy explains what the app does and
does not do with your information. It is written to be read, not to be survived.

## The short version

The app itself collects nothing. Your settings never leave your phone. The only third parties
involved are Google's advertising and payment services, and they only apply if you use the free
tier or make a purchase.

---

## What the app stores on your device

Everything the app remembers is stored locally, on your phone, and is deleted when you uninstall:

- Your filter settings (strength, dim, green tint, warmth) and any presets you save
- Whether the filter is currently on
- Your schedule (start time, end time, days of the week)
- Your theme choice and whether you have completed the intro

None of this is transmitted anywhere. There is no account, no login, and no server belonging to us.

## What the app does **not** do

- It does not read, record, or transmit the contents of your screen. The green tint is drawn *on
  top of* the display; the app cannot see what is underneath it.
- It does not collect health information. You never tell it anything about your migraines.
- It does not use your location, camera, microphone, contacts, or files.
- It does not track you across other apps or websites.

## Advertising (free tier only)

The free tier shows a single banner advertisement, served by **Google AdMob**. To do this, Google
may process device identifiers and ad interaction data. Google acts as an independent data
controller for that processing.

- Where the law requires it (the EEA, the UK, and Switzerland), you are shown a consent form
  before any ad is requested, and you can change your answer at any time via
  **Settings → Ad privacy options**.
- Purchasing Migraine Relief Pro removes ads entirely, and no ad requests are made thereafter.
- Google's practices are described at
  [policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites](https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites).

## Purchases

Purchases are processed by **Google Play Billing**. We never see or store your payment details.
The app asks Google only one question — whether this Google account owns Migraine Relief Pro — and
stores nothing about you as a result.

## Crash reporting

If crash reporting is enabled in a release, the app uses **Firebase Crashlytics** to record
diagnostic information when it crashes (device model, OS version, and the stack trace). This is
used solely to fix defects. It contains no health data and nothing that identifies you personally.

## Children

The app is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect data from them.

## Your rights

Because we hold no data about you, there is nothing for us to export or delete on your behalf.
Uninstalling the app removes everything it stored. For ad-related data, use the in-app **Ad
privacy options** entry, or Google's own controls.

## Not a medical device

Migraine Relief is a screen-comfort filter. **It is not a medical device, and it does not provide
medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.** If you have migraine or any other health concern,
please speak to a qualified healthcare professional.

## Changes

If this policy changes materially, the updated version will be published here and the date at the
top will change.

